            "columns_description" :
              [
                "This column was automatically created in order to record in what polygon from the dataset 'US House Districts for PA 2019 Health' (gbji-5m4q) the point in column 'georeferenced_latitude_longitude_2' is located.  This enables the creation of region maps (choropleths) in the visualization canvas and data lens.",
                "A unique concatenation of the nearest PennDOT linear reference location for entrance to the Park and Ride derived from PennDOT’s RMSSEG database. The elements are: \n•\tcounty code (2)\n•\tstate route number (4)\n•\troute segment number (4)\n•\toffset from the beginning of the segment, in feet (4)\n",
                "Traffic route designation. I=Interstate, US=Unites States, PA=Pennsylvania",
                "Exit number appearing on signage in the primary linear referencing direction. The absence of a number indicates the exit is unnumbered.",
                "Flag indicating the availability of transit at or near the lot. The absence of a flag indicates transit availability is unknown, Y=YES.",
                "Flag indicating SPACES were determined by remote sensing means, Y=YES. All remotely sensed data was derived from ortho-photography captured between 2010 and 2017. Scale = 1:2,400.",
                "The number of parking spaces available at the lot, including handicapped.",
                "Flag indicating designated handicapped parking is available. The absence of a flag indicates handicapped parking availability is unknown, Y=YES.",
                "Longitude expressed as decimal degrees derived from ortho-photography captured between 2010 and 2017. Scale = 1:2,400.",
                "PennDOT Engineering District number responsible for the Park and Ride.",
                "",
                "The number of handicapped spaces at the Park and Ride. All handicapped spaces are approximated through remote sensing means. All remotely sensed data was derived from ortho-photography captured between 2010 to 2017. Scale = 1:2,400.",
                "The owner or lessor of the lot.",
                "Flag indicating the Park and Ride is open for use, Y=YES, N=NO",
                "State route number assigned to the Park and Ride. A Null value indicates no route number has been assigned.",
                "Flag indicating official PennDOT Park and Ride, Y=YES.",
                "A textual description of the Park and Ride’s area served and street location.",
                "Latitude expressed as decimal degrees derived from ortho-photography captured between 2010 and 2017. Scale = 1:2,400.",
                "A unique identifier for each Park and Ride",
                "Supplemental textual description information.",
                "The traffic route where sign exit name and exit number is installed",
                "This column was automatically created in order to record in what polygon from the dataset 'PA State House Districts 2016 Health' (its3-bt6a) the point in column 'georeferenced_latitude_longitude_2' is located.  This enables the creation of region maps (choropleths) in the visualization canvas and data lens.",
                "This column was automatically created in order to record in what polygon from the dataset 'PA County Boundaries Spatial Data Current Transportation' (4fjn-fq7k) the point in column 'georeferenced_latitude_longitude_2' is located.  This enables the creation of region maps (choropleths) in the visualization canvas and data lens.",
                "This column was automatically created in order to record in what polygon from the dataset 'US House Districts for PA 2019' (3x3q-vpda) the point in column 'georeferenced_latitude_longitude_2' is located.  This enables the creation of region maps (choropleths) in the visualization canvas and data lens.",
                "Route direction from which the exit name and the exit number was captured",
                "Exit ‘for’ location(s) appearing on signage on the exit route. ",
                "PennDOT’s numeric county identifier for the Park and Ride’s location.  County code and County Name: 01 ADAMS, 02 ALLEGHENY, 03 ARMSTRONG,\t04 BEAVER, 05 BEDFORD, 06 BERKS, 07 BLAIR, 08 BRADFORD, 09 BUCKS, 10 BUTLER, 11 CAMBRIA, 12 CAMERON, 13 CARBON, 14 CENTRE, 15 CHESTER, 16 CLARION, 17 CLEARFIELD, 18 CLINTON, 19 COLUMBIA, 20 CRAWFORD, 21 CUMBERLAND, 22 DAUPHIN, 23 DELAWARE, 24 ELK, 25 ERIE, 26 FAYETTE, 27 FOREST, 28 FRANKLIN, 29 FULTON, 30 GREENE, 31 HUNTINGDON, 32 INDIANA, 33 JEFFERSON, 34 JUNIATA, 35 LACKAWANNA, 36 LANCASTER, 37 LAWRENCE, 38 LEBANON, 39 LEHIGH, 40 LUZERNE, 41 LYCOMING, 42 MCKEAN, 43 MERCER, 44 MIFFLIN, 45 MONROE, 46 MONTGOMERY, 47 MONTOUR, 48 NORTHAMPTON, 49 NORTHUMBERLAND, 50 PERRY, 51 PIKE, 52 POTTER, 53 SCHUYLKILL, 54 SNYDER, 55 SOMERSET, 56 SULLIVAN, 57 SUSQUEHANNA, 58 TIOGA, 59 UNION, 60 VENANGO, 61 WARREN, 62 WASHINGTON, 63 WAYNE, 64 WESTMORELAND, 65 WYOMING, 66 YORK, 67 PHILADELPHIA",
                "This column was automatically created in order to record in what polygon from the dataset 'PA State Senate Districts 2016 Health' (75dh-jrw3) the point in column 'georeferenced_latitude_longitude_2' is located.  This enables the creation of region maps (choropleths) in the visualization canvas and data lens."
